The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = kobject_init_and_add(&type->kobj, &mdev_type_ktype, NULL, "%s-%s", dev_driver_string(parent->dev), group->name);
if (ret) {
    kfree(type);
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when `kobject_init_and_add()` fails, it returns an error code, but the original code incorrectly uses `kfree(type)` to free the memory allocated for `type`. This does not account for the reference taken by `kobject_init_and_add()`, leading to a memory leak since the kobject is not properly released.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = kobject_init_and_add(&type->kobj, &mdev_type_ktype, NULL, "%s-%s", dev_driver_string(parent->dev), group->name);
if (ret) {
    kobject_put(&type->kobj);
}
```
Reason:
The fix replaces `kfree(type)` with `kobject_put(&type->kobj)`, which correctly decrements the reference count of the kobject. This ensures that if `kobject_init_and_add()` fails, the memory associated with the kobject is properly released, preventing the memory leak.

